# SHA256SUMS -- known-good checksum for the ONNX model used by the onnx mode.
#
# download.sh verifies the downloaded file against this list and deletes the
# partial download on mismatch, so a corrupted or tampered model can never be
# silently loaded.
#
# Provenance: the Ultralytics YOLOv8n export at 320x320:
#     from ultralytics import YOLO
#     YOLO("yolov8n.pt").export(format="onnx", imgsz=320, opset=13,
#                               simplify=False, dynamic=False)
#   with ultralytics 8.4.120 / torch 2.13.0.
#
# 320 rather than the default 640: inference cost scales with the square of
# the input size, and 640 was unusably slow on a Raspberry Pi 4. The model
# resolution must match src/core/image_ops.hpp's kInputSize.
#
# This digest only applies to a file fetched with `download.sh --fetch` from a
# URL you host. It is NOT reproducible by exporting locally: ONNX export is not
# bit-deterministic, so even on the exact versions above a fresh export lands
# on a different digest. Measured: 9cc4ded5... recorded, f7fd6c4e... re-exported
# on identical ultralytics/torch.
#
# That is harmless, because nothing downstream depends on the bytes. The
# autotuning database in models/tuning/ keys on the lowered TIR graph, so it
# applies to any export of this model at this input size -- verified by
# regenerating against a fresh export and getting the same 87 parallel /
# 158 vectorized schedules.
#
# Re-exporting with a different version or size changes the digest:
#     shasum -a 256 models/onnx/yolov8n.onnx
#
# Format: <sha256hex>  <filename>   (two spaces, GNU sha256sum compatible)

9cc4ded538798c658726518ef94f7c505a58743fd01c7b0cfe58a8258bdf8e62  yolov8n.onnx
